WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.335
-My first guest is
one of my favorites.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.337
She is a Golden Globe-winning
actress

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.840
starring in a new film
called "Yes Day,"

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.574
which premieres
on Netflix tomorrow.

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:10.743
Here is Jennifer Garner!

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.512
Ah, come on.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.847
Ah, the best!
-Come on, Jimmy!

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:16.449
-Welcome back.
-Oh!

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:19.019
-Thank you.
-I'm so happy to see you, buddy.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.920
-I'm so happy
to see you, too, bud.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.688
You recently posted a photo

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:26.659
with your "13 Going on 30"
costar Mark Ruffalo,

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.161
and the Internet broke in half.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:31.064
They went crazy.
We have that photo.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.965
You guys just --
-Aw.

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:35.801
-You guys just wrapped
another movie together

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.237
called "The Adam Project."

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:40.006
What was it like working
together again?

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:43.042
-It was so instantly comfortable

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:45.745
and there was just
so much trust there.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:48.948
There's just nothing like having
known people for a long time.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.984
You know, there's nothing
like -- it made you feel

00:00:51.984 --> 00:00:55.121
more brave and it made you
feel really safe.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.388
It was lovely.

00:00:56.388 --> 00:00:59.125
I just loved being
with Mark again.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.860
-And also, Ryan Reynolds
is in the movie.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:05.298
Let me just say, if I could sit
at a table with you,

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:09.235
Mark Ruffalo, and Ryan Reynolds,
that's the best table.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.571
I mean, you're three of
the most talented people,

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:15.474
but also funny,
but also giving and caring.

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:18.110
What was Ryan like?

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:21.748
-Well, first of all --
Well, there's also Zoe Saldana

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.849
and Catherine Keener,
so it's just an amazing --

00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:25.552
it's such a cool cast
to be a part of.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.519
-Oh, my gosh.
-But it is going to be

00:01:27.519 --> 00:01:28.955
such a special movie.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.489
I cannot wait
for you guys to see it.

00:01:30.489 --> 00:01:32.926
We're all used to
laughing at Ryan,

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.828
but just have
a box of tissues ready

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.996
'cause he's gonna tear your
heart out and feed it to you.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.599
-Really?
-Yeah. He's a killer.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:42.802
He's my son.
You know, he's Mark and my son.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:45.171
Little baby Ryan Reynolds.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.606
That's perfect, man.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.007
That is great.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.775
I have to say, your new movie

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:53.378
"Yes Day" comes out
on Netflix tomorrow.

00:01:53.378 --> 00:01:55.181
This is really your baby.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.483
Not only do you star in it,
but you produced it as well.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.985
Congrats on that.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.054
I think it's a perfect movie
for you.

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:05.524
I think in my head -- and I may
be wrong -- that that is you --

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:07.292
I think you'd be
the best mom ever.

00:02:07.292 --> 00:02:09.329
I think you're so fun.

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.597
-Oh, my gosh. I don't know.

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.398
I think the whole point
of "Yes Day"

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:16.703
is because no matter what, moms
stop being fun all the time.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.405
We just, like, kind of
turn into a drag,

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:21.274
just being like,
"Do you have your socks on?

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:22.442
Have you brushed your teeth?

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.443
Do you have your soccer cleats
for later?"

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:27.680
And you just get kind of
robotic and rigid

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.981
trying to make it all happen.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:31.884
So my kids, I started doing
a yes day with my kids

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.721
when, really, a long time ago
because my daughter loved

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:37.924
Amy Krouse Rosenthal --
beautiful angel --

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:40.059
her book "Yes Day" so much.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.395
Kids books make
such a difference, Jimmy.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:44.663
Just wait till I get to make
one of yours into a movie.

00:02:44.663 --> 00:02:46.299
I'll be so excited.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:49.168
-It's a two-word movie.

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:50.636
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:53.239
But my daughter loved the book
so much,

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.475
she begged for a yes day,
and we did it,

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:57.309
and then we started doing
them as a tradition,

00:02:57.309 --> 00:03:00.179
once a year, the kids and I
would, for nine years.

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:01.680
And now, here it is.
It's a movie.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.318
And I can't wait for people to
see it because it really is fun

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:08.488
and joyful and after a year
of just solid no,

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.790
it's just a big, fat, juicy yes.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.325
-[ Laughs ] Exactly.

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:14.894
The other thing is how many
times you actually have to say

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:18.898
no in the movie, and you do
it -- every one is different.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:21.400
But you're like,
"No, no, nope, no."

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.669
And then, there's one you say
that's stuck in my head.

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:26.472
You go, "Nope on a rope.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.040
Nope on a rope."

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.743
I just -- That one crushed me.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.845
-Try it.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.447
I'm offering for all of America.

00:03:35.447 --> 00:03:40.186
Please try "nope on a rope,"
because it's no, but it's kicky.

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.854
-Yeah, it's got
a little kick to it, yeah.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.189
"No. Nope."
-It's got a little kick.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.924
-Nope on a rope, yeah.
-Nope on a rope.

00:03:45.924 --> 00:03:49.896
-Was there anything doing this
movie that made you turn around

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.163
and say -- wish you said no?

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:52.798
You go,
"Yeah, I said yes to that.

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:53.966
I should have said no."

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:55.801
-I don't like singing
in front of people,

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:58.037
and I sing in
this stinking movie.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:00.272
And actually, I don't think --
I don't know if I'm allowed

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:05.510
to say this, but I'm going to
just break a rule and tell you,

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.446
H.E.R. is in our film,

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:11.650
and H.E.R. plays music
in our film and has a scene.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:13.686
She is incredible.
-A genius.

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:17.323
-She's the most unbelievable --
and her band is there as well.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:22.328
And then, I had to sing with
H.E.R., the H.E.R., yes.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.529
-No, no, no.
No, that's pressure.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.097
-Yeah, I can't even
think about it.

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:27.500
I can't -- I went out --
I had to say to the audience

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.802
beforehand, I had to say like,

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.637
"I don't like to sing
in front of people.

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:33.806
You're all here. We have to
get through this together.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:36.175
If I pee my pants, have just --

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.243
we're just going to
have a laugh.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.544
I don't know
what's gonna happen.

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:39.945
We just have to
get through it together.

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:42.314
So God bless you."
-I thought you nailed it.

00:04:42.314 --> 00:04:44.850
I also want to say,
we were talking earlier

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.186
and I said like,
"I wish people could see this,"

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.754
you know, in a crowd,
and you were like,

00:04:48.754 --> 00:04:52.090
"Yeah, weirdly, we tested it
with families through TVs,"

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:54.761
and they let you watch them
react to the movie

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:56.095
so you can edit
and stuff like that?

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.363
-It was amazing!

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.265
Like, I've never tested a movie
like this,

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:02.067
but it's Netflix and you're
supposed to watch it at home.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.469
There was a pandemic.

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:07.707
So we had cameras up on their --
we were able to watch

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:09.041
the families watching the movie,

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:10.776
and they would be
leaving the room,

00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:13.312
grabbing popcorn, all laughing,
doing what they do.

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:17.015
But as the movie came to
the third act, everyone --

00:05:17.015 --> 00:05:21.754
and I was watching 150 families
screening through Zoom screens

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.822
and watching them get
closer and closer

00:05:23.822 --> 00:05:25.557
till they were huddled up
on the couch

00:05:25.557 --> 00:05:26.993
and the moms,
like, wiping a tear.

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:29.729
And we were like,
"Yes, we did it! We did it."

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:31.463
It was the best.
That's all you want.

00:05:31.463 --> 00:05:34.634
You just want, like, my goal
is for there to be families

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.335
all over the world
cuddled up on the couch

00:05:36.335 --> 00:05:37.436
by the end of the movie.

00:05:37.436 --> 00:05:39.138
-I want to show a clip
from the movie.

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:41.474
Here's Jennifer Garner
in "Yes Day."

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:42.908
Take a look.

00:05:42.908 --> 00:05:45.644
-I'm sorry, but you got to
make it through a yes morning,

00:05:45.644 --> 00:05:48.247
let alone a yes day.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:51.984
-Would you like to have
a little wager on that?

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:53.886
-You know what? I would love to.

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:55.287
How about this?

00:05:55.287 --> 00:05:58.190
If you say no one time,

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.858
I get to go to Flea Fest
with Layla.

00:05:59.858 --> 00:06:01.327
No adults, no parents.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:04.130
Just us young, underage,
vulnerable girls.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.099
-Wait, honey, are you sure?

00:06:07.099 --> 00:06:09.202
-I'll take your wager, missy,

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:11.236
because I know that
I won't say no.

00:06:11.236 --> 00:06:13.573
And when you lose --
and you will lose --

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:17.943
I am so fun that you will still
get to go to your concert.

00:06:17.943 --> 00:06:19.611
-Really?
-Absolutely.

00:06:19.611 --> 00:06:21.214
With me!

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:23.849
I'm gonna sit right next to you
and we're gonna hold hands

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:26.386
and we're gonna put our hands in
the air like we just don't care.

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:30.656
-Jennifer Garner, everybody.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:33.226
"Yes Day" premieres tomorrow
on Netflix.

